Z||000000||JSocha||11-01-2001||10:16 PM||||I don't know if it is just me or not, but I just noticed something in a few other threads and comparing it since I had first gotten here and registered.<P>Seems like people are still feeling uneasy (to be expected from...as of late) and as if they need to tramp lightly as if walking on the proverbial egg shells.<P>I think most of us are mature enough around here to realize that yes, there are some of the occasional "Rabble Rousers" who show up just to stir up trouble and/or severely disagree with others, but all in all everyone comes out or still remains friends.<P>I don't know about everyone else, as everyone else is different.  However, just to clear the air and so that everyone else realizes, I'm typically a very laid back individual and don't take offense to much that is posted.  I get a chuckle and don't take what one says personally.  Not like some  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> did.<P>Anyways, I know it is going to take some time to reach some sort of normalacy around here again.  I also hope that sharing how I typically take things can start the healing process.  Besides, when is the last time I jumped somebody's ship (albeit one) for sharing their opinion?  Even FUNGUY had his rights and yes, I did get out of line there, which can happen with anyone.  It is just realizing that its happening and that one needs to pull back.<P>Anyways...sorry so long winded.  I just want others to feel comfortable in responding to my posts and that I typically, if not the majority of the time...do not take offense to what may be posted.  You all be and are cool in my book.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Have to go back upstairs now as it is bill paying night as I just got paid yesterday.  Anybody got a real heavy boulder I can put on my checkbook?  It's getting awfully light and needs some weight to hold it down.  I would sit on it, however, one side of my butt starts to lift off the chair...||||reg||6
