Z||000016||maryjane||11-03-2001||10:47 AM||||First, JSocha, you DO know I was joking about you being a troublemaker, I hope.<BR>The problem doesn't come from controversial topics being mounted; trouble starts from lack of respect and personalities getting involved. I personally like to read other's beliefs and opinions on things. I like being goaded and pushed along to understand where people are coming from with things. I don't have to agree, just accept the fact that people are not of one frame of thought. After a long discussion with RayB, concerning religion, I now understand what he means and a little of where he originates his ideals. I also realize he a is pretty darn intelligent and well researched person. I don't agree with everything he believes, but have respect for those beliefs. That's really all we can ever really expect from one another. The hardest things we learn are the mistakes we make on our own. The easiest and often, best, things we learn, are the things we learn from others. Tolerance and respect are the key things to keep in mind when talking about things that we may not personally agree with. I'm guilty of not following this at times, and most of us are. <BR>Again, Cliff, thanks for this space and all the work & expense that goes into it. I don't think that's cheerleadin, just a little<BR>well deserved respect.<BR>Don<BR><p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-03-2001).]||||reg||1
